; ==============================================================================
; ipip Daemon Configuration Template
; ==============================================================================
; This template configures the ipip daemon. ipip (IPIP) is an IPIP tunnel driver
; for Amprnet/AMPR networks. It handles tunneling IP packets over IPIP tunnels.
;
; The configuration is split into two parts:
; 1. Global flags passed to the daemon at startup.
; 2. Specific arguments passed only when the daemon starts (start_flags).
;
; NOTE: The actual network interfaces (tunnels) are typically defined by
;       external scripts or systemd service arguments, as this specific
;       daemon format is quite legacy and interface-heavy. However, the
;       flags below control general behavior.

; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Global Flags
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Default flags passed to the ipip daemon (e.g., 'defaults 50').
; These flags apply to the daemon process as a whole.
; Example: "defaults 50" sets default parameters for new tunnels.
; See the ipip man page for available global flags.
{{ flags | default('defaults 50') }}

; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Start Flags
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Additional arguments passed specifically when starting the daemon.
; These are appended to the command line invocation of the ipip daemon.
; Use this to pass specific startup options not covered by global flags.
; Example: "--verbose" or "--pidfile /run/ipip.pid"
; Leave empty if no additional startup arguments are needed.
{% if start_flags is defined and start_flags != "" %}
{{ start_flags }}
{% endif %}